  Input bytes:

  "hello" = 68 65 6c 6c 6f

  Final result will be:

  SHA256("hello")
  = 2cf24dba5fb0a30e26e83b2ac5b9e29e1b161e5c1fa7425e73043362938b9824

  1. Pad The Message

  SHA-256 works on 64-byte / 512-bit chunks.

  Original message length:

  5 bytes = 40 bits = 0x28

  Padding rule:

  message
  + 0x80
  + zero bytes until byte length is 56 mod 64
  + original bit length as 8-byte big-endian integer

  So "hello" becomes one 64-byte chunk:

  68656c6c6f8000000000000000000000
  00000000000000000000000000000000
  00000000000000000000000000000000
  00000000000000000000000000000028

  2. Split Into 16 Words

  SHA-256 treats the chunk as sixteen 32-bit big-endian words:

  W[00] = 68656c6c
  W[01] = 6f800000
  W[02] = 00000000
  W[03] = 00000000
  W[04] = 00000000
  W[05] = 00000000
  W[06] = 00000000
  W[07] = 00000000
  W[08] = 00000000
  W[09] = 00000000
  W[10] = 00000000
  W[11] = 00000000
  W[12] = 00000000
  W[13] = 00000000
  W[14] = 00000000
  W[15] = 00000028

  Then SHA-256 expands these to 64 words. For example:

  W[16] = 7594884c
  W[17] = 6f910000
  W[18] = d532d15a
  W[19] = a01bde7a
  ...
  W[63] = derived value

  Expansion formula:

  W[i] = σ1(W[i-2]) + W[i-7] + σ0(W[i-15]) + W[i-16]

  where additions wrap at 32 bits.

  3. Initial State

  SHA-256 starts with eight fixed 32-bit values:

  H0 = 6a09e667
  H1 = bb67ae85
  H2 = 3c6ef372
  H3 = a54ff53a
  H4 = 510e527f
  H5 = 9b05688c
  H6 = 1f83d9ab
  H7 = 5be0cd19

  These become working variables:

  a = H0
  b = H1
  c = H2
  d = H3
  e = H4
  f = H5
  g = H6
  h = H7

  4. Compression Rounds

  SHA-256 runs 64 rounds.

  Each round computes:

  T1 = h + Σ1(e) + Ch(e,f,g) + K[i] + W[i]
  T2 = Σ0(a) + Maj(a,b,c)

  h = g
  g = f
  f = e
  e = d + T1
  d = c
  c = b
  b = a
  a = T1 + T2

  After round 0, the state is:

  a = 646df4b9
  b = 6a09e667
  c = bb67ae85
  d = 3c6ef372
  e = 012d4f0e
  f = 510e527f
  g = 9b05688c
  h = 1f83d9ab

  After round 1:

  a = a01b3ad4
  b = 646df4b9
  c = 6a09e667
  d = bb67ae85
  e = 27198bd1
  f = 012d4f0e
  g = 510e527f
  h = 9b05688c

  After round 2:

  a = 46a5c0f7
  b = a01b3ad4
  c = 646df4b9
  d = 6a09e667
  e = 0fbadb9b
  f = 27198bd1
  g = 012d4f0e
  h = 510e527f

  This continues through round 63.

  After the final round, the working state is:

  a = c2e86753
  b = a448f489
  c = ea7947b8
  d = 2069ed64
  e = ca07cbdd
  f = 84a1d9d2
  g = 538059b7
  h = 37aacb0b

  5. Add Back Into Initial State

  Now SHA-256 adds the working state back into the original H0..H7 values:

  H0 = 6a09e667 + c2e86753 = 2cf24dba
  H1 = bb67ae85 + a448f489 = 5fb0a30e
  H2 = 3c6ef372 + ea7947b8 = 26e83b2a
  H3 = a54ff53a + 2069ed64 = c5b9e29e
  H4 = 510e527f + ca07cbdd = 1b161e5c
  H5 = 9b05688c + 84a1d9d2 = 1fa7425e
  H6 = 1f83d9ab + 538059b7 = 73043362
  H7 = 5be0cd19 + 37aacb0b = 938b9824

  All additions are modulo 2^32.

  Concatenate them:

  2cf24dba
  5fb0a30e
  26e83b2a
  c5b9e29e
